A||N||6||Chris McDonald||87-88 H/L motor-description please||||5||
Z||000000||Chris McDonald||08-17-2001||08:18 PM||||As mentioned before, I am working on a special project.  <P>I need to know some things about the 87-88 H/L motors (two wire hook up).<P>Do they use a nut or pin to secure the first actuator lever to the motor shaft?  I know for a fact that the 84-86 motors used a nut.<P>Do you know the G.M. part number for the right and left hand motor?  (The original and whatever new updated number they have been given)<P>Are all three of the mounting holes threaded, or is the top one just drilled out smooth?<P>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Songman||08-18-2001||02:18 AM||||They use a nut to attach the linkage to the motor shaft.<P>Don't have any idea about the part numbers.<P>And yes, all three mounting holes are threaded.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Chris McDonald||08-18-2001||05:10 AM||||Hmmmmm,<P>I wonder how easy/hard it is to buy them new?  I know my local parts guy did not have any in stock.  They are the largest G.M. parts distributors in the southeast, but did not even have the late design C4 in stock (which I thought were identical to the late Fiero).<P>The typical junk yard Fiero has long since been robbed of the light motors.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Songman||08-18-2001||10:30 AM||||They are the same motors as late model Firebirds. Much more plentiful and probably cheaper as well. Not sure of the exact years but I imagine it the same years as Fieros would work... 87 up till ???<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||7
Z||000004||KissMySSFiero||08-18-2001||10:49 AM||||there is a junkyard in jax area that has them.  if you know the yard off of joe johns road they have them in there on an 88 coupe.  let me know if you want to know where they are in the yard.  they were there as of late june.  also they have a set of ttops in there but they are very rough.  the seals are wasted(i tried to pull them off but they were on with some strong epoxy.)  i cant get any of the stuff because i no longer live in the area.   let me know if you want to go out there.  <BR>ssfiero@aol.com<BR><P>------------------<BR>JOEJOE Aol:SSFiero <P>88FORMULA<BR>      <A HREF="mailto:SSFiero@Aol.com">SSFiero@Aol.com</A>       <P>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FORUMSIG1.jpg">           <BR>"Kids in the backseat cause accidents,  accidents in the backseat caused me!!"||||reg||1
Z||000005||Chris McDonald||08-18-2001||07:09 PM||||I went to U Pull a Part off Normandy this morning.  Picket up two perfect new style actuator motors and a handfull of other parts including several control modules.  <P>Thanks for the input.  <P>I don't think $10 per motor was a bad deal.  <P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Songman||08-18-2001||09:08 PM||||Nope.. not a bad deal at all...<P>Didn't even notice you were from Florida.. Someone else for me to meet when we come down. My girlfriend is from Jacksonville and we are down often to visit her Dad.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||14
